### Ejecutar primero usersservice (8081) y plazoletaservice (8082).
### Cambiar email/documento si ya existen, y copiar el id de la respuesta en ownerId.
@usersUrl = http://localhost:8081/api/v1/users
@restaurantsUrl = http://localhost:8082/api/v1/restaurants
@ownerId = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_OWNER_UUID

### Crear propietario - 201
POST {{usersUrl}}/owners
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana",
  "lastName": "Perez",
  "document": "987654321",
  "phone": "+573001234567",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01",
  "email": "ana.hu2@example.com",
  "password": "ExamplePassword123"
}

### Validar propietario - 200, exists=true y owner=true
GET {{usersUrl}}/{{ownerId}}/owner-validation

### Crear restaurante - 201, devuelve UUID y los datos guardados
POST {{restaurantsUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pizza 123",
  "nit": "900123456",
  "address": "Calle 10 #20-30",
  "phone": "+573001234567",
  "urlLogo": "https://example.com/logo.png",
  "ownerId": "{{ownerId}}"
}

### Usuario inexistente - 400 (usar un UUID que no exista)
POST {{restaurantsUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pizza 123",
  "nit": "900123456",
  "address": "Calle 10",
  "phone": "3001234567",
  "urlLogo": "https://example.com/logo.png",
  "ownerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Nombre numerico con espacios - 400 sin consultar usuarios
POST {{restaurantsUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": " 123 ",
  "nit": "900123456",
  "address": "Calle 10",
  "phone": "3001234567",
  "urlLogo": "https://example.com/logo.png",
  "ownerId": "{{ownerId}}"
}

### Direccion vacia - 400
POST {{restaurantsUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pizza",
  "nit": "900123456",
  "address": " ",
  "phone": "3001234567",
  "urlLogo": "https://example.com/logo.png",
  "ownerId": "{{ownerId}}"
}

### UUID mal formado - 400
GET {{usersUrl}}/invalid/owner-validation

### Para comprobar 503: detener usersservice y repetir la creacion valida.
### Para comprobar rol incorrecto: usar el UUID de un CLIENT/EMPLOYEE/ADMIN existente.
### OpenAPI
GET http://localhost:8082/v3/api-docs
